cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in academic or technical work, please cite it as below."
title: "conformal-margin"
abstract: >-
  Fleet-level security monitoring for AI agent deployments with formal
  False-Positive-Rate guarantees via split conformal prediction. The library
  composes robust nonconformity scoring (median + scaled MAD), inductive
  conformal calibration with exact rank statistics, and Page-Hinkley drift
  detection. Architecturally committed to detection without enforcement.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Rodewald"
    given-names: "Gabriel"
    affiliation: "Silency Technologies"
    website: "https://silency.io"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-05-15"
url: "https://github.com/silencytechnologies/conformal-margin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/silencytechnologies/conformal-margin"
license-url: "https://github.com/silencytechnologies/conformal-margin/blob/main/LICENSE"
keywords:
  - conformal-prediction
  - anomaly-detection
  - agentic-ai
  - ai-security
  - robust-statistics
  - drift-detection
  - page-hinkley
  - false-positive-rate
  - calibration
  - distribution-free
references:
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: "Vovk"
        given-names: "Vladimir"
      - family-names: "Gammerman"
        given-names: "Alexander"
      - family-names: "Shafer"
        given-names: "Glenn"
    title: "Algorithmic Learning in a Random World"
    publisher:
      name: "Springer"
    year: 2005
    doi: "10.1007/b106715"
    notes: >-
      Foundational text for conformal prediction. The split conformal
      construction and exact coverage guarantee used in this library
      originate here.

  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: "Shafer"
        given-names: "Glenn"
      - family-names: "Vovk"
        given-names: "Vladimir"
    title: "A Tutorial on Conformal Prediction"
    journal: "Journal of Machine Learning Research"
    volume: 9
    start: 371
    end: 421
    year: 2008
    notes: >-
      Accessible introduction to conformal prediction; recommended starting
      point for readers new to the framework.

  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: "Angelopoulos"
        given-names: "Anastasios N."
      - family-names: "Bates"
        given-names: "Stephen"
    title: "Conformal Prediction: A Gentle Introduction"
    journal: "Foundations and Trends in Machine Learning"
    volume: 16
    issue: 4
    start: 494
    end: 591
    year: 2023
    doi: "10.1561/2200000101"
    notes: >-
      Modern, practitioner-oriented introduction to conformal prediction
      covering split conformal, classification, regression, and the
      distinction between marginal and conditional coverage.

  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: "Vovk"
        given-names: "Vladimir"
    title: "Conditional Validity of Inductive Conformal Predictors"
    journal: "Machine Learning"
    volume: 92
    issue: "2-3"
    start: 349
    end: 376
    year: 2012
    doi: "10.1007/s10994-013-5355-6"
    notes: >-
      Cited for the distinction between marginal and conditional coverage.
      The bound implemented in this library is marginal; readers should
      understand the implications of that choice.

  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: "Huber"
        given-names: "Peter J."
      - family-names: "Ronchetti"
        given-names: "Elvezio M."
    title: "Robust Statistics"
    edition: "2"
    publisher:
      name: "Wiley"
    year: 2009
    isbn: "978-0-470-12990-6"
    notes: >-
      Canonical reference for robust estimators including the median
      absolute deviation used in the RobustScorer component.

  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: "Leys"
        given-names: "Christophe"
      - family-names: "Ley"
        given-names: "Christophe"
      - family-names: "Klein"
        given-names: "Olivier"
      - family-names: "Bernard"
        given-names: "Philippe"
      - family-names: "Licata"
        given-names: "Laurent"
    title: >-
      Detecting outliers: Do not use standard deviation around the mean,
      use absolute deviation around the median
    journal: "Journal of Experimental Social Psychology"
    volume: 49
    issue: 4
    start: 764
    end: 766
    year: 2013
    doi: "10.1016/j.jesp.2013.03.013"
    notes: >-
      Practitioner-oriented argument for replacing mean+std with
      median+MAD in outlier detection. Directly motivates the
      RobustScorer design choice.

  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: "Page"
        given-names: "E. S."
    title: "Continuous Inspection Schemes"
    journal: "Biometrika"
    volume: 41
    issue: "1/2"
    start: 100
    end: 115
    year: 1954
    doi: "10.2307/2333009"
    notes: >-
      Original formulation of the Page-Hinkley sequential change-point
      test used by the DriftDetector component.

  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: "Gama"
        given-names: "João"
      - family-names: "Žliobaitė"
        given-names: "Indrė"
      - family-names: "Bifet"
        given-names: "Albert"
      - family-names: "Pechenizkiy"
        given-names: "Mykola"
      - family-names: "Bouchachia"
        given-names: "Abdelhamid"
    title: "A Survey on Concept Drift Adaptation"
    journal: "ACM Computing Surveys"
    volume: 46
    issue: 4
    start: 1
    end: 37
    year: 2014
    doi: "10.1145/2523813"
    notes: >-
      Comprehensive survey of drift detection methods. Establishes the
      taxonomy from which the one-directional Page-Hinkley choice is
      made in this library.

  - type: conference-paper
    authors:
      - family-names: "Han"
        given-names: "Songqiao"
      - family-names: "Hu"
        given-names: "Xiyang"
      - family-names: "Huang"
        given-names: "Hailiang"
      - family-names: "Jiang"
        given-names: "Minqi"
      - family-names: "Zhao"
        given-names: "Yue"
    title: "ADBench: Anomaly Detection Benchmark"
    collection-title: "Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems"
    volume: 35
    year: 2022
    notes: >-
      Reference benchmark suite for anomaly detection methods. Cited as
      the kind of empirical validation conformal-margin has not yet
      undergone; future work.